        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Cliff Richard, David Kossoff, Lauri Peters, Melvyn Hayes, Teddy Green, Jeremy Bulloch, Una Stubbs, Pamela Hart, Jacqueline Daryl, Lionel Murton, Madge Ryan, Nicholas Phipps, Ron Moody, Alec Clunes, Bass\n- Works: Summer Holiday, The Young Lovers, The Next Time, Bachelor Boy, The Bespoke Overcoat\n- Groups: The Shadows\n- Places: London, Arts Theatre\n- Topics: British musical films, BAFTA awards, number-one singles\n\nFacts:\n- David Kossoff was born on 24 November 1919 and was a British actor.\n- In 1954, David Kossoff won a BAFTA for his appearance in The Young Lovers.\n- Summer Holiday is a 1963 British CinemaScope and Technicolor musical film featuring singer Cliff Richard.\n- The cast of Summer Holiday includes Lauri Peters, Melvyn Hayes, Teddy Green, Jeremy Bulloch, Una Stubbs, Pamela Hart, Jacqueline Daryl, Lionel Murton, Madge Ryan, David Kossoff, Nicholas Phipps, Ron Moody, and The Shadows.\n- The Next Time, backed with Bachelor Boy, was the first of three number-one hit singles from the Cliff Richard musical Summer Holiday.\n- The play The Bespoke Overcoat was performed at the Arts Theatre in London with Kossoff and Bass and was directed by Alec Clunes.\n- David Kossoff died on 23 March 2005.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
